{"name":"US Air Force Blue","hex":"#00308f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"air","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Airoran."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The substance constituting Earth's atmosphere: a gaseous mixture of nitrogen, oxygen, and various trace gases.","The substance of the atmosphere seen as an agency of freshness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/air"},{"term":"force","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ability to influence; strength or energy of body or mind; active power; vigour; might; capacity of exercising an influence or producing an effect.","A physical quantity that denotes ability to push, pull, twist or accelerate a body and which has a direction and is measured in a unit dimensioned in mass × distance/time² (ML/T²): SI: newton (N); CGS: dyne (dyn)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make someone or something do something, often regardless of their will.","To constrain by force; to overcome the limitations or resistance of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/force"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Air Force Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Air Force Blue is an American-bred, Irish-trained Thoroughbred racehorse. As a juvenile in 2015 he established himself as the best two-year-old colt in Europe by recording three consecutive Group One wins in the Phoenix Stakes, National Stakes and Dewhurst Stakes. On his reappearance in 2016 he was unplaced when odds-on favourite for the 2000 Guineas, was well beaten in the Irish 2,000 Guineas on his second start and suffered two further defeats over shorter distances before being retired to stud."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Owner_Mrs_John_Magnier.svg/330px-Owner_Mrs_John_Magnier.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_Force_Blue","wikidata":"Q22006584"},{"title":"Air Force blue","blocks":[{"text":"Air Force blue colours are a variety of colours that are mostly various tones of the colour azure, the purest tones of which are identified as being the colour of the sky on a clear day."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/RAF_Thornycroft_Antar_Lorry_-_tank_transporter.jpg/330px-RAF_Thornycroft_Antar_Lorry_-_tank_transporter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_Force_blue","wikidata":"Q1770362"},{"title":"Force Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Force Blue is a trawler-expedition style luxury yacht built by Royal Denship in 2002."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Force_Blue_IMO_1007524_in_Monaco.jpg/330px-Force_Blue_IMO_1007524_in_Monaco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Force_Blue","wikidata":"Q5467433"},{"title":"Air force","blocks":[{"text":"An air force in the broadest sense is the national military branch that primarily conducts aerial warfare. More specifically, it is the branch of a nation's armed services that is responsible for aerial warfare as distinct from an army aviation or naval aviation units. Typically, air forces are responsible for gaining control of the air, carrying out strategic and tactical bombing missions, and providing support to land and naval forces often in the form of aerial reconnaissance and close air support."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Usaf.f15.f16.kc135.750pix.jpg/330px-Usaf.f15.f16.kc135.750pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_force","wikidata":"Q61883"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Tupolev_Tu-22M3_at_Ryazan_Dyagilevo.jpg/500px-Tupolev_Tu-22M3_at_Ryazan_Dyagilevo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Tupolev_Tu-22M3_at_Ryazan_Dyagilevo.jpg/1280px-Tupolev_Tu-22M3_at_Ryazan_Dyagilevo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Tupolev_Tu-22M3_at_Ryazan_Dyagilevo.jpg/500px-Tupolev_Tu-22M3_at_Ryazan_Dyagilevo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATupolev_Tu-22M3_at_Ryazan_Dyagilevo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/PLAAF_Changhe_WZ-10_-_Jordan.jpg/500px-PLAAF_Changhe_WZ-10_-_Jordan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/PLAAF_Changhe_WZ-10_-_Jordan.jpg/500px-PLAAF_Changhe_WZ-10_-_Jordan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APLAAF_Changhe_WZ-10_-_Jordan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/TAI_Anka.jpg/500px-TAI_Anka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/TAI_Anka.jpg/1280px-TAI_Anka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/TAI_Anka.jpg/500px-TAI_Anka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail"